Subject: main: on OpenVMS, keep the program name "flex"

flex takes its name for messages and --version from argv[0].  On VMS
that is the image's file specification ("FLEX.EXE", or a full
"dev:[dir]FLEX.EXE;1"), so --version printed "FLEX.EXE 2.6.4".  Keep
the built-in "flex" there.

--- a/src/main.c	2026-10-04 23:16:57.489772374 +0100
+++ b/src/main.c	2026-10-04 23:16:57.490494774 +0100
@@ -1018,7 +1018,11 @@
     flex_init_regex();
 
 	/* Enable C++ if program name ends with '+'. */
+#ifndef __VMS
+	/* On VMS argv[0] is the image's file specification ("FLEX.EXE" or
+	   "dev:[dir]FLEX.EXE;1"); keep the name "flex" for messages.  */
 	program_name = basename (argv[0]);
+#endif
 
 	if (program_name != NULL &&
 	    program_name[strlen (program_name) - 1] == '+')
